---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/facts';
import { CONSENT_TEXT } from '../config/consent';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — iphoneduo.live"
  description="What this site collects: server logs, an optional email list stored on Cloudflare D1, and cookieless analytics."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <article class="px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>

      <p class="text-muted">
        This is a small independent site. It does what is described below and nothing else.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Who runs it</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contact}`} class="text-ink underline decoration-line"
          >{SITE.contact}</a
        > with any question about this page, or to ask for your data to be deleted.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Server logs</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        The site is hosted on Cloudflare, which logs requests — including IP address, user
        agent and the page requested — as part of serving and protecting the site. Cloudflare
        holds those logs under its standard retention. We do not build profiles from them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-semibold">The email list</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        If you enter your address in the signup form, we store it in a Cloudflare D1 database
        that we control, along with the time you signed up, your IP address and your browser's
        user agent. The last two exist to spot abuse of the form.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        You are agreeing to this, which is the wording shown next to the checkbox:
        <span class="mt-2 block border-l-2 border-line pl-4 text-ink">{CONSENT_TEXT}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        We do not sell, rent or share the list with third parties. Every email we send carries a
        one-click unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing takes effect immediately.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        Visits are counted by Umami, which runs on our own server at analytics.yilmaz.games.
        It sets no cookies and records no personal data, so it runs without asking you first
        and the data never leaves our hands.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        We also use Google Analytics. That one sets cookies in your browser and sends data to
        Google, which may process it outside your country.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        None of that happens unless you allow it. Analytics is denied by default, and the
        Google Analytics script is not downloaded at all until you press Accept on the
        banner. Press Decline and no request is ever made to Google. You can change your
        answer later with the "Cookie settings" button in the corner of any page.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted">
        The one thing we keep in your browser without asking is your answer to that banner,
        so you are not asked again on every visit. It is not shared with anyone.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Deleting your data</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        Use the unsubscribe link in any email, or write to <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.contact}`}
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line">{SITE.contact}</a
        > and we will remove your address from the database.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
